{"name":"Hazelnut Parfait","hex":"#d9be9d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hazelnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit of the hazel, especially of species Corylus avellana, which is grown commercially.","A light tan color inspired by the color of hazelnut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hazelnut"},{"term":"parfait","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A French parfait (parfait glacé), an iced dessert made with egg yolks, sugar, cream, and flavouring (usually fruit), sometimes with the addition of a liqueur.","An American parfait, a layered dessert often consisting of fruit, ice cream, pastries, whipped topping, etc. and served in a glass, often a parfait glass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parfait"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hazelnut","blocks":[{"text":"The hazelnut is the fruit of the hazel tree and therefore includes any of the nuts deriving from species of the genus Corylus, especially the nuts of the species Corylus avellana. They are also known as cobnuts or filberts according to species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg/330px-Hazelnuts_%28Corylus_avellana%29_-_whole_with_kernels.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazelnut","wikidata":"Q578307"},{"title":"Parfait","blocks":[{"text":"Parfait is either of two types of dessert. In France, where the dish originated, parfait is made by boiling cream, egg, sugar and syrup to create a custard-like or meringue-like puree which is then frozen. The American version consists of layers differentiated by the inclusion of such ingredients as granola, nuts, yogurt and liqueurs, topped off with fruits or whipped cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parfait_samples_by_pinguino_in_Osaka%2C_Japan.jpg/330px-Parfait_samples_by_pinguino_in_Osaka%2C_Japan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parfait","wikidata":"Q13314"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Haselnuss.jpg/500px-Haselnuss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Haselnuss.jpg/500px-Haselnuss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cracked hazelnut shell displaying the edible seed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaselnuss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG/500px-Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG/1280px-Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG/500px-Corylus_colurna_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hazelnut tree, Turkey","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorylus_colurna_(1).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Corylus_maxima_fruit.jpg/500px-Corylus_maxima_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Corylus_maxima_fruit.jpg/1280px-Corylus_maxima_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Corylus_maxima_fruit.jpg/500px-Corylus_maxima_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hand-harvest and sun-drying of hazelnuts in Turkey","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w